{"resource":{"id":"go-answer-key","title":"Go — Answer Key","category":"Programming","difficulty":"Beginner","readingTime":"25 min","pages":44,"lastUpdated":"April 2026","tags":["Programming","Go","Concurrency"],"heroImage":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1461749280684-dccba630e2f6?w=1800&q=80","heroSubtitle":"The full Answer Key for the Go Practice Questions workbook — worked solutions, alternate approaches, optimisations, and evaluation rubrics."},"toc":[{"id":"objectives","label":"Learning Objectives"},{"id":"s1","label":"1. MCQ Answers"},{"id":"s2","label":"2. Fill-in Answers"},{"id":"s3","label":"3. Debugging Solutions"},{"id":"s4","label":"4. Output Explanations"},{"id":"s5","label":"5. Coding Walkthroughs"},{"id":"s6","label":"6. Concurrency Solutions"},{"id":"s7","label":"7. Mini-Project Reviews"},{"id":"s8","label":"8. Scenario Answers"},{"id":"s9","label":"9. Evaluation Rubric"},{"id":"review","label":"Answer Review"},{"id":"faqs","label":"FAQ"},{"id":"glossary","label":"Glossary"},{"id":"references","label":"References"},{"id":"disclaimer","label":"Disclaimer"}],"related":[{"title":"Go — Practice Questions","tag":"Programming","time":"31 min"},{"title":"Go — Interview Questions","tag":"Programming","time":"26 min"},{"title":"Go — Complete Tutorial","tag":"Programming","time":"55 min"}],"html":"<section id=\"objectives\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Learning Objectives</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li>Confirm answers to the Practice Questions workbook.</li>\n          <li>Learn multiple approaches per problem — not just one solution.</li>\n          <li>Understand time and space trade-offs.</li>\n          <li>Use the evaluation rubric to self-assess objectively.</li>\n        </ul>\n        <div class=\"my-4 rounded-2xl border-l-4 border-amber-500/40 bg-amber-500/10 text-amber-900 dark:text-amber-100 p-4\"><div class=\"flex items-start gap-3\"><div class=\"mt-0.5 shrink-0\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"h-5 w-5\"><path d=\"M15 14c.2-1 .7-1.7 1.5-2.5 1-.9 1.5-2.2 1.5-3.5A6 6 0 0 0 6 8c0 1 .2 2.2 1.5 3.5.7.7 1.3 1.5 1.5 2.5\"/><path d=\"M9 18h6\"/><path d=\"M10 22h4\"/></svg></div><div class=\"min-w-0 flex-1\"><p class=\"text-sm font-semibold\">Don&#x27;t peek</p><div class=\"mt-1 text-sm\">Only open this after a genuine attempt — otherwise the practice value collapses.</div></div></div></div>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s1\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">1. MCQ Answers</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <table class=\"w-full border-collapse text-sm\">\n          <thead><tr class=\"border-b\"><th class=\"p-2 text-left\">#</th><th class=\"p-2 text-left\">Answer</th><th class=\"p-2 text-left\">Why</th></tr></thead>\n          <tbody>\n            <tr class=\"border-b\"><td class=\"p-2\">1</td><td class=\"p-2\">(b) go</td><td class=\"p-2\">The keyword launches a goroutine.</td></tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b\"><td class=\"p-2\">2</td><td class=\"p-2\">(c) false</td><td class=\"p-2\">Zero value of bool.</td></tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b\"><td class=\"p-2\">3</td><td class=\"p-2\">(a) encoding/json</td><td class=\"p-2\">Standard-library package.</td></tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b\"><td class=\"p-2\">4</td><td class=\"p-2\">(a) ptr, len, cap</td><td class=\"p-2\">Slice header struct.</td></tr>\n            <tr><td class=\"p-2\">5</td><td class=\"p-2\">(b) channel</td><td class=\"p-2\">Channels transfer both data and synchronisation.</td></tr>\n          </tbody>\n        </table>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s2\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">2. Fill-in Answers</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ol class=\"list-decimal space-y-1 pl-5 text-sm\">\n          <li><code>package main</code></li>\n          <li><code>:=</code></li>\n          <li><code>sync.WaitGroup</code></li>\n          <li><code>context.Context</code></li>\n          <li><code>range</code></li>\n        </ol>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s3\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">3. Debugging Solutions</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p><strong>#1</strong> — unbuffered channel: send blocks. Fix by buffering or launching a receiver first.</p>\n        <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>python</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>ch := make(chan int, 1)\nch &lt;- 1\nfmt.Println(&lt;-ch)</code></pre></div>\n        <p><strong>#2</strong> — data race on <code>count</code>. Fix with <code>sync.Mutex</code> or <code>atomic.AddInt64</code>.</p>\n        <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>python</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>var count int64\nfor i := 0; i &lt; 100; i++ {\n  go func(){ atomic.AddInt64(&amp;count, 1) }()\n}</code></pre></div>\n        <p><strong>#3</strong> — writing to a nil map panics. Initialise it first with <code>make</code>.</p>\n        <Figure src=\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1517694712202-14dd9538aa97?w=1400&q=80\" caption=\"Figure 1 — Every fix ships with a regression test — otherwise the bug is coming back.\" />\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s4\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">4. Output Explanations</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p><strong>Slice aliasing:</strong> assigning a slice shares the backing array — mutating <code>t</code> mutates <code>s</code>.</p>\n        <p><strong>Loop closure:</strong> pre-Go 1.22, <code>i</code> and <code>v</code> were shared across iterations; Go 1.22+ gives each iteration a fresh variable.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s5\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">5. Coding Walkthroughs</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p><strong>LRU cache</strong> — O(1) get/put using a hash map + doubly linked list. Head = most recent, tail = eviction victim.</p>\n        <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>python</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>type entry struct{ k, v int; prev, next *entry }\ntype LRU struct {\n  cap int\n  m   map[int]*entry\n  h,t *entry\n}\n// … Get/Put move touched entry to head; Put evicts tail when full.</code></pre></div>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s6\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">6. Concurrency Solutions</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p><strong>Bounded worker pool</strong> — N goroutines each range over a shared jobs channel, results written to another channel.</p>\n        <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>python</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>for i := 0; i &lt; N; i++ {\n  go func(){\n    for j := range jobs { results &lt;- work(j) }\n  }()\n}</code></pre></div>\n        <Figure src=\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1544197150-b99a580bb7a8?w=1400&q=80\" caption=\"Figure 2 — Fan-out / fan-in with buffered channels keeps memory bounded and workers busy.\" />\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s7\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">7. Mini-Project Reviews</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li><strong>URL shortener</strong>: base62 encoding, collision handling, 302 redirects, Prometheus metrics.</li>\n          <li><strong>Log tailer</strong>: <code>fsnotify</code> for file changes, regex compiled once, backpressure on slow consumers.</li>\n          <li><strong>Chat server</strong>: hub goroutine owns clients map; per-connection read + write goroutines.</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s8\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">8. Scenario Answers</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p><strong>Memory leak:</strong> capture heap profiles, diff over time, look for growing goroutine counts, confirm exit paths.</p>\n        <p><strong>Slow dependency:</strong> retry with jittered exponential backoff, wrap in a circuit breaker, and add a shorter timeout than the caller expects.</p>\n        <p><strong>10× traffic:</strong> check p99 latency by handler, DB connections, GC pauses, and outbound network egress before assuming code is the culprit.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s9\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">9. Evaluation Rubric</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <table class=\"w-full border-collapse text-sm\">\n          <thead><tr class=\"border-b\"><th class=\"p-2 text-left\">Criterion</th><th class=\"p-2 text-left\">Weight</th></tr></thead>\n          <tbody>\n            <tr class=\"border-b\"><td class=\"p-2\">Correctness</td><td class=\"p-2\">40%</td></tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b\"><td class=\"p-2\">Idiomatic Go</td><td class=\"p-2\">25%</td></tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b\"><td class=\"p-2\">Complexity</td><td class=\"p-2\">15%</td></tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b\"><td class=\"p-2\">Tests</td><td class=\"p-2\">15%</td></tr>\n            <tr><td class=\"p-2\">Docs</td><td class=\"p-2\">5%</td></tr>\n          </tbody>\n        </table>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"review\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Answer Review</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <h3 class=\"font-semibold\">Final Revision</h3>\n        <p>Re-solve any question you scored below 70% on. Aim for 3 rounds before moving on.</p>\n        <h3 class=\"mt-3 font-semibold\">Performance Report</h3>\n        <p>Weakest chapters usually appear in concurrency and error wrapping — focus practice there.</p>\n        <h3 class=\"mt-3 font-semibold\">Improvement Suggestions</h3>\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li>Read one open-source Go package per week.</li>\n          <li>Rewrite the LRU cache in 3 different ways.</li>\n          <li>Pair-review your own code after 48 hours.</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"faqs\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">FAQ</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <details class=\"group my-2 rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-card p-4 open:shadow-sm\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 text-sm font-semibold\"><span>Are alternate solutions accepted?</span><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition group-open:rotate-90\"><path d=\"m9 18 6-6-6-6\"/></svg></summary><div class=\"mt-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground\">Yes — favour readable over clever if performance is comparable.</div></details>\n        <details class=\"group my-2 rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-card p-4 open:shadow-sm\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 text-sm font-semibold\"><span>What if my answer differs from the key?</span><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition group-open:rotate-90\"><path d=\"m9 18 6-6-6-6\"/></svg></summary><div class=\"mt-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground\">Explain your reasoning — if it holds, it's a valid alternative.</div></details>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"glossary\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Glossary</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li><strong>Rubric</strong> — scoring framework with weighted criteria.</li>\n          <li><strong>Jitter</strong> — random variance in backoff to avoid retry storms.</li>\n          <li><strong>Circuit breaker</strong> — trip open when a dependency fails repeatedly.</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"references\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">References</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\"><References /></div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"disclaimer\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Disclaimer</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p class=\"text-sm text-muted-foreground\">\n          Answer Key for educational purposes. Multiple valid solutions may exist; consult official\n          docs for canonical patterns. Trademarks belong to their respective owners.\n        </p>\n      </div></section>"}